{"type": "tool_call", "n": 10, "ts": 1790151729.396399, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "MEMO \u2014 Halvard Systems Inc. (US, USD): March 2026 Revenue by Stream\nPrepared 2026-04-03 for the CFO. Read-only analysis; no entries posted, reversed, matched or flagged. All figures in USD, from the US ledger, period 2026-03.\n\nSUMMARY\n  Subscription Revenue (4000) .......... $52,300.00\n  Usage Revenue (4100) ..................  $   977.00\n  Professional Services Revenue (4200) .  $ 7,500.00\n  ---------------------------------------------------\n  TOTAL MARCH 2026 REVENUE ............. $60,777.00\n\nEach stream total equals the period activity on its GL account (get_account_balance, US, 2026-03) and equals the sum of the individual journal entries listed below. No unexplained differences.\n\nTRAIL \u2014 SUBSCRIPTION REVENUE (4000): $52,300.00\n  JE-00222  2026-03-01  INV-2111  Acme Logistics   Subscription \u2013 March 2026   +18,000.00\n  JE-00224  2026-03-01  INV-2113  Corvid Retail    Subscription \u2013 March 2026   +11,500.00\n  JE-00219  2026-03-01  INV-2115  Fairview Labs    Subscription \u2013 March 2026    +9,400.00\n  JE-00215  2026-03-01  INV-2112  Beacon Health    Subscription \u2013 March 2026    +8,000.00\n  JE-00225  2026-03-01  INV-2114  Evergreen Bank   Subscription \u2013 March 2026    +6,200.00\n  JE-00275  2026-03-20  CM-0031   Beacon Health    SLA credit (credit memo)       -800.00\n  Gross invoiced $53,100.00 less credit memo $800.00 = $52,300.00. Ties to 4000 period activity (-52,300.00 Dr-Cr).\n  All six entries: source AR, status posted, support attached. Beacon Health net for March = $7,200.00.\n\nTRAIL \u2014 USAGE REVENUE (4100): $977.00\n  JE-00236  2026-03-04  INV-2180  Acme Logistics   API usage overage Feb          +977.00\n  Ties to 4100 period activity (-977.00). Source AR, posted, support DOC-0164.\n\nTRAIL \u2014 PROFESSIONAL SERVICES REVENUE (4200): $7,500.00\n  JE-00255  2026-03-10  INV-2118  Fairview Labs    Implementation services \u2013 March 2026   +7,500.00\n  Ties to 4200 period activity (-7,500.00). Source AR, posted, support attached.\n\nOBSERVATIONS (for awareness only; nothing changed)\n1. Usage revenue is recognized on invoice date, one month in arrears: the $977 booked in March is February API overage (INV-2180), and the February usage entry (JE-00130, INV-2120, $844) followed the same pattern. There is no unbilled/contract-asset accrual for March usage in the March ledger, so March consumption will land in April revenue when billed. Consistent policy month to month, no double count, but the CFO should read the \"usage\" line as a one-month lag if comparing to platform consumption data. If a true-up to a consumption basis is wanted, that would be an accrual policy decision for the controller.\n2. The Beacon Health SLA credit (CM-0031, $800) reduces subscription revenue in March. Presented net above; gross subscription billings were $53,100.\n3. Intercompany management fee income (4800) and interest income (4900) are excluded from the above per the request (customer revenue streams only).\n4. Cumulative YTD balances at 31-Mar-2026 for reference: 4000 $158,500; 4100 $2,433; 4200 $22,500 (credit balances).\n\nNo exceptions raised; no checklist items changed.\n"}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 8}
